## Benchmark results (amd64, i9-11900K @ 3.5 GHz)

BenchmarkPunycodeEncode-16     15,764,258 iters     92.34 ns/op    45 B/op    1 allocs/op
BenchmarkPunycodeDecode-16     15,524,508 iters     80.14 ns/op    60 B/op    1 allocs/op

## Key algorithm choices (C++ line references)

Punycode.cpp lines 25-33   — RFC 3492 §5 parameters (base=36, tmin=1, tmax=26,
                             skew=38, damp=700, initial_bias=72, initial_n=128,
                             delimiter='_'). Reproduced verbatim as Go consts.

Punycode.cpp lines 35-48   — Custom alphabet:
                             digitValue: digit<26 → 'a'+digit; else 'A'-26+digit
                             digitIndex: 'a'-'z' → 0-25; 'A'-'J' → 26-35; else -1
                             (NOT standard base-36 '0'-'9' for high digits)

Punycode.cpp lines 50-53   — isValidUnicodeScalar: accepts 0xD800-0xD87F for
                             non-symbol ASCII remapping (mapNonSymbolChars path).

Punycode.cpp lines 58-71   — Bias adaptation function (RFC 3492 §6.1).
                             Firsttime divides by damp=700, otherwise by 2.

Punycode.cpp lines 75-144  — Decode: find last delimiter, copy ASCII prefix,
                             then bias-adaptive variable-length integer decoding,
                             insert each decoded scalar at position i in output.
                             Overflow guards mirror the C++ int32 max checks.

Punycode.cpp lines 148-212 — Encode: copy ASCII to output, append delimiter if b>0,
                             then for each non-basic scalar in increasing order emit
                             a bias-adaptive variable-length integer delta.

Punycode.cpp lines 276-283 — decodePunycodeUTF8 = decodePunycode + encodeToUTF8.
                             In Go we combine both steps in PunycodeDecode.

Punycode.cpp lines 214-274 — encodeToUTF8: 0xD800-0xD87F mapped back to ASCII
                             (S -= 0xD800). Reproduced in codePointsToUTF8.

Note: PunycodeEncode does NOT implement mapNonSymbolChars remapping (the
$e embedded-ABI path). Non-symbol ASCII is passed through unchanged. This
matches the default (mapNonSymbolChars=false) path in encodePunycodeUTF8.
